UNIT adopt_kept_content
LANG js
PRIMARY-SHA256 f12abd39c819e36f544857da0f077f9d078ddb864b0e67ccf6ab80e83e8b7ecc
SIG adopt_kept_content(unmanaged: string, managed: string): string[]
NOTE default export
ABI text = string (UTF-16 code units; the only length test, the ONE-LINE FENCE's > 6, means "a non-empty middle", so
  no unit counting is observable; every pinned set is BMP); list[text] = a fresh Array of strings.
  The artifact is an ES module default-exporting the function and importing nothing.
ENVELOPE widening: a non-text argument throws, as the package does — managed is read first (a null, number or other
  non-string managed throws a TypeError from its first string operation), then unmanaged. Only the fact of the throw is
  graded, not the message (the two non-text probes at the end of the curated prefix).
MECHANISM the package's own forms realize the primary exactly: LF-READ and R2 = text.split('\n') with each line
  replace(/\r$/, ''); unmanaged R1 = rejoin with '\n' then trim(); managed R1 = rejoin, match BEGIN and slice after it,
  then match END and slice before it, then String.prototype.trim (whose set is BLANK); ONE-LINE FENCE = ONELINE.test(line)
  and line.trim().length > 6; FENCE LINE = FENCE.test(line) and not ONE-LINE FENCE; RUN = FENCE_RUN.exec(line)?.[1] ?? '';
  CLOSES = RUN(line) non-empty, same first character and at least as long as RUN(opener), and
  line.trim().slice(RUN.length).trim() empty; HEADING, LIST as the pins below with
  String.prototype.match (no m, s or u flag: \s is BLANK, the dot excludes NOTDOT and LF, $ is the end of the line);
  heading body = group 2 trimmed, list BODY = group 2 untrimmed; fragments = when RAW.test(body): [body.trim()] minus empties;
  otherwise body.replace(MASK, push the span and return '\u0000' + index + '\u0000'), split(SPLIT), each
  piece replace(UNMASK, (_, k) => spans[Number(k)]), trim, drop empties; KEY = when RAW.test(fragment): '\u0002' + fragment; otherwise split(CODESPAN) (the
  capture group keeps the spans), a part that starts and ends with a backtick and has length at least 2 -> '\u0001' + slice(1, -1) +
  '\u0001', any other part -> toLowerCase(), join(''), replace(/\s+/g, ' '), trim(); LINE KEY =
  replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim(); each PROSE LIST is an Array of KEYs, R9's test a contiguous-window comparison at every
  start index; KEY LINES = [line] for a one-element ONE-LINE FENCE; [opener, ...slice(1, -1) minus blank lines] when
  length > 1 and CLOSES(opener, last line); otherwise [];
  the BLOCK KEYs a Set.
DEPENDS-ON none
PINNED regex BEGIN = /<!--\s*rederive:begin\b(?:(?!<!--)[\s\S])*?-->/ CITED R1 — adopt.mts BEGIN_RE (managed text only)
PINNED regex END = /<!--\s*rederive:end\s*-->/ CITED R1 — adopt.mts END_RE (managed text only)
PINNED regex FENCE = /^\s*(?:```|~~~)/ CITED R2 — adopt.mts isFence (and not ONELINE)
PINNED regex FENCE_RUN = /^\s*(`{3,}|~{3,})/ CITED R2 — adopt.mts fenceRun, closesFence
PINNED regex ONELINE = /^\s*```.*```\s*$/ CITED R4 — adopt.mts isOneLineFence (and line.trim().length > 6)
PINNED regex HEADING = /^(#{1,6})\s+(.+)$/ CITED R4 — adopt.mts HEADING_RE
PINNED regex LIST = /^\s*(\d+\.|[-*])\s+(.*)$/ CITED R5 — adopt.mts extractItems
PINNED regex MASK = /`[^`]*`/g CITED R6 — adopt.mts splitSentences, each match replaced by '\u0000' + index + '\u0000'
PINNED regex SPLIT = /(?<=[.!?]["')\]]?)\s+(?=[A-Z`(\u0000])/ CITED R6 — adopt.mts splitSentences
PINNED regex UNMASK = /\u0000(\d+)\u0000/g CITED R6 — adopt.mts splitSentences, replaced by spans[Number(k)]
PINNED regex RAW = /[\u0000\u0001]/ CITED R6 R7 — adopt.mts splitSentences and normalizeForMatch, the uncut raw branch
PINNED regex CODESPAN = /(`[^`]*`)/ CITED R7 — adopt.mts normalizeForMatch
PROVENANCE rederive@c7b0916ed08a cli/lib/adopt.mts — this file states the type mapping and the dialect only; no behavior.
